{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-13-6","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：黄金分割与截差无理线段与无理线段","englishTitle":"If a rational straight line be cut in extreme and mean ratio, each of the segments is the irrational straight line called apotome.","book":13,"number":6,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":6,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","contentId":"euclid-13-6","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c601907a7e21590a875fbb19aa16033a8514ae5c1661c14cdba374bdc1e026c5","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-13-6.statement","euclid-13-6.construction.1","euclid-13-6.construction.2","euclid-13-6.proof.1","euclid-13-6.proof.2","euclid-13-6.proof.3","euclid-13-6.proof.4","euclid-13-6.proof.5","euclid-13-6.proof.6","euclid-13-6.proof.7","euclid-13-6.proof.8","euclid-13-6.conclusion","euclid-13-6.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-13-6.statement","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a3f9dc0634139db1d115805d4a40d0f1b47634cd474cef54eda696cde7a95df6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If a rational straight line be cut in extreme and mean ratio, each of the segments is the irrational straight line called apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果有理线段分之一在黄金分割分, 每一部分是无理线段分, 叫做截差无理线段分。"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"816c16d38429bd47d934039081a4bddf061bcce9d3bb253a96b020a4aad5eedd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let AB be a rational straight line, let it be cut in extreme and mean ratio at C, and let AC be the greater segment; I say that each of the straight lines AC, CB is the irrational straight line called apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让AB成为有理线段,让它在黄金分割时在C分切割,让AC分成为较大的数量部分;我说,AC直线中的每一条直线都是无理线段,称为截差无理线段。（相关点与线段：CB）"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a5c2e613816ecc818ed1abaf40832fd2bd734ce2b4c55749ebcd01b8f8f6ec36","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let BA be produced, and let AD be made half of BA."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"延长BA,将BA的一半定为AD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"449ef25ec9570441a435cc3c48ae8f62575e1aeac2c28c781307a000843bfded","citations":["euclid-13-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then the straight line AB has been cut in extreme and mean ratio, and to the greater segment AC is added AD which is half of AB, therefore the square on CD is five times the square on DA. [[XIII. 1](/principles/euclid-13-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"自此,直线 AB在黄金分割被削减,在较大的数量部分AC中,增加了AD,即AB的一半,因此,CD的正方形是DA的正方形的5倍。 [[XIII. 1](/principles/euclid-13-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fa70ea026f84940f7ff3f6a79dd1abd23eaf56516142f21e7f76e364fafb6f76","citations":["euclid-10-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the square on CD has to the square on DA the ratio which a number has to a number; therefore the square on CD is commensurable with the square on DA. [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,CD的正方形与DA的比是正方形,数字是CD的正方形,而DA的比是可公度。 [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"174f54b52c60708bf15774894f8322ebf4d9195ad69c6bb88b41f3b24fe28cdc","citations":["euclid-10-def-4"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the square on DA is rational, for DA is rational, being half of AB which is rational; therefore the square on CD is also rational; [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)] therefore CD is also rational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但DA的正方形是有理,DA是有理,是AB的半数,即有理;因此,CD的正方形也是有理;因此,CD也是有理。 [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4376b6bce0cb68fb451948fd70923a1569b93d5fe96df64c81c95852cc911ef1","citations":["euclid-10-9","euclid-10-73"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, since the square on CD has not to the square on DA the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore CD is incommensurable in length with DA; [[X. 9](/principles/euclid-10-9)] therefore CD, DA are rational straight lines commensurable in square only; therefore AC is an apotome. [[X. 73](/principles/euclid-10-73)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由于CD的正方形比DA的正方形比平方数比平方数,CD比不可公度,DA比CD;CD比有理线段,平方可公度而长度不可公度,AC比截差无理线段。 [[X. 9](/principles/euclid-10-9)] [[X. 73](/principles/euclid-10-73)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d0b4b177358712d2b09add00a99df914f58d8f1df39b85fd91220823708a1a00","citations":["euclid-6-def-3","euclid-6-17"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Again, since AB has been cut in extreme and mean ratio, and AC is the greater segment, therefore the rectangle AB, BC is equal to the square on AC. [[VI. Def. 3](/principles/euclid-6-def-3), [VI. 17](/principles/euclid-6-17)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,由于黄金分割削减了AB,AC是较大的数量部分,因此,矩形 AB,BC等于AC的正方形个 [ [VI. Def. 3](/principles/euclid-6-def-3) [VI. 17](/principles/euclid-6-17)"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"56162d78fd73391197946056f66815994255c185647dadcdc8fb8045043ab2cb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the square on the apotome AC, if applied to the rational straight line AB, produces BC as breadth."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,截差无理线段 AC上的正方形如果适用于有理线段 AB,则宽度为BC。"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"187fe8b7098db5c4f0b8ce04c82a829c333eb406e8efeb51bf417467a6e8d342","citations":["euclid-10-97"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the square on an apotome, if applied to a rational straight line, produces as breadth a first apotome; [[X. 97](/principles/euclid-10-97)] therefore CB is a first apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是截差无理线段机上的正方形如果应用到有理线段, 则生成第截差无理线段机的宽度, 因此, CB是第截差无理线段机的宽度。 [[X. 97](/principles/euclid-10-97)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9212a2e87d9f7045a0aa98a69dac06a4826834d9d53cfc27e7480d7ae76efd7b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And CA was also proved to be an apotome."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"CA 也被证明是截差无理线段"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":11,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-13-6.source","contentId":"euclid-13-6","revisionId":"euclid-13-6@raw-c601907a7e21590a","order":12,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"58c8ebcf09c37b60eb87c97b02af34dafb7a85382af06d6c038411956f4a38f7","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-13-6:euclid-13-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-13-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-13-6.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-13-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6/","sourceLabel":"XIII. 1"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-13-6:euclid-10-6:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-13-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-13-6.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-6","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6/","sourceLabel":"X. 6"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-13-6:euclid-10-def-4:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-13-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-13-6.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-def-4","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:13.prop.6","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.